so one of the things that i think is  misunderstood about leadership is that  it's not just from the top leaders have  to set set the environment for sure and  leaders have to uh uh  lead by example for sure  but you know this is our organization  this is your organization like you don't  get to nobody gets to sit on the  sidelines and be like all right what  have you done for me lately right um you  know i don't even mind negativity you  know you know people like oh my goodness  that person's such a negative nelly but  because sometimes negative people who  are in the fight and they're still  willing to they show up every day  they're great you know it's it's when  people are negative and they just stand  on the sides and throw stones and there  and i don't mean like bring me solutions  that's not what i mean i mean just like  you're in it you're in the scrum and and  you're willing to be a part of it so  like you have to come to work here every  day there's a there's a great story when  gordon bethune took over continental  airlines which was what  which existed prior to united  um they merged um it was a terrible  airline it was the worst rated airline  in the country for every every metric  and one of the things that was bad was  the planes were always dirty  and the the customers would always  complain and they would always get  yelled at by management clean the planes  for the customer the customers are  complaining and when gordon bethune  showed up he said forget about the  customer they're on the plane they're  off the plane in three hours you have to  do four you're gonna have to do four  more flights before your shift is done  why don't you clean the plane for  yourselves like this is your office like  once you keep it nice for yourself  in fact there's a there's a funny  statistic between ups trucks and u.s  postal service trucks which is u.s post  u.s um postal service trucks um uh i  think they only last about two years  before they have to be replaced  and ups trucks last something like five  years before they have to get replaced  ups they clean their trucks every single  day and u.s postal service trucks they  clean their trucks once a week  because when you give somebody something  really nice to work in they look after  it  and so like it becomes incumbent upon  all of us to say this is when we're  talking about leadership which is if you  see someone struggling go to them if you  see someone who's unhappy maybe you know  go to them if somebody's stuck in a  false narrative maybe help them change  their narrative give them a safe space  to feel heard sometimes people just need  to empty their bucket some people  sometimes just need to vent and get it  all out and then they're actually fine  and sometimes what we do by mistake is  trying to interrupt them correct the  facts fix the problem  and so we can be that like you can be  that for the people you work with that's  a huge part of it like taking  responsibility for the organization in  which you work yes leadership does bear  some responsibility of course but i  think everybody in the organization is  included in that as well we want people  not to just fit the culture but to be  additive and contribute to the culture
 

